// render.js - every picture of the engine that is kept as a PNG in Base64 inside a source file
// (static const wxString s_<name>_png = "..."), drawn again from its SVG. The code that reads a picture does not
// change: only the text between the quotes does.
//
//   node tools/pictures/render.js            draws every target below and writes it into its source file
//   node tools/pictures/render.js --check    draws nothing; says which targets are missing or not found
//   node tools/pictures/render.js <name>...  draws only the targets whose source key or variable is named
//
// THE SOURCE OF A PICTURE IS ITS SVG, here in SOURCES; the PNG in the source file is made from it. Change a picture:
// edit its SVG below, run this. Add one: an SVG below, a line in TARGETS, and the string in the file that reads it
// (any placeholder that starts iVBORw0KGgo will do - this fills it in).
//
// THE PNG IS A MASTER, four times the SVG's own grid (a 16 px drawing is kept at 64 px, a 12 px one at 48): whoever
// reads it scales it down to the size it shows it at (GetIconFromBase64(..., wxSize(16, 16)), the art provider by the
// size asked, RegisterBackendPicture to 16) - so the picture stays sharp on a display scaled to 125 or 200 %.
// (A variable's name may still say 16 or 64: the size the code first asked for, not the size of the master.)
//
// The manner every SVG follows is the debugger's: a 16x16 grid, strokes 1-2 with round ends, straight edges on whole
// pixels, the Open Color palette - blue #1c6fd1 an action, green #2f9e44 adding, red #e03131 taking away, grey
// #495057 a thing, #868e96 text. Families share a base (a field is a plate, a register a square, a catalog or a chart
// a book) and show their kind by a sign on it; one act has one drawing everywhere it appears.
//
// The PNG is made by a headless Microsoft Edge (EDGE overrides where it lives), on a transparent ground.

